   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Stage\n\nA long page on a perspective studio plane, with the camera travelling across it on keyframes. The plane holds a built-in placeholder page drawn in CSS; to use your own, replace the markup inside #st-page in the file (it is 1265 wide and 5000 tall, scaled to the plane).\n\nCategory: layout. Length: 10 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A product screen, website or image should read as a photographed object rather than a flat full-frame capture.\n- The camera needs to travel across one continuous surface, including a page much taller than the frame.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You only need a full-frame fill or rounded inset with no 3D presentation: use backdrop.\n- You are moving between two scenes: use a transition. Elements inside the subject need independent depth: Stage treats the page as one flat plane.\n\nVariables:\n- preset (enum): Camera path, default \"smooth-descent\"\n- shake (number, 0-1): Handheld shake, default 0\n- seed (string): Shake seed, default \"smooth-descent\"\n- backdrop (string): Backdrop, default \"linear-gradient(145deg, #17181d 0%, #09090b 72%)\"\n- rotate_x (number, -180-180): Rotate X, default 14\n- rotate_y (number, -180-180): Rotate Y, default -20\n- perspective (number, 50-5000): Perspective, default 900\n- scale (number, 0.1-3): Scale, default 0.86\n- radius (number, 0-4): Radius, default 1.4\n- reflection (number, 0-1): Reflection, default 0.24\n- shadow (number, 0-1): Contact shadow, default 0.7\n- light (number, 0-1): Studio light, default 0.55\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
